@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam roundcorner 18
title LoginAttempt - Derived Lockout State Machine
state "No attempt row" as Absent
state "Available\nlocked_until = null" as Available
state "Locked\nlocked_until > now" as Locked
state "Expired, pending next attempt\nlocked_until <= now" as Expired
[*] --> Absent
Absent --> Available : login POST / get_or_create(username)
Available : authenticate [success] / failures=0; save
Available : authenticate [failure and failures+1 < limit] / failures++; save
Available -down-> Locked : authenticate [failure and failures+1 >= limit]\n/ failures++; locked_until=now+lock_minutes; save
Locked : login POST [now < locked_until] / render retry-later; skip authentication
Locked -down-> Expired : at(locked_until)
Expired -left-> Available : next login POST\n/ clear failures and lock; evaluate credentials
Available --> Absent : reset / delete row
Locked --> Absent : reset / delete row
Expired --> Absent : reset / delete row
note bottom of Expired
  These states are derived from fields and current time,
  not stored enum values. Expiration has no background timer:
  the next login request performs cleanup and authentication.
end note
note bottom of Available
  Authentication result also depends on password and User.is_active.
  Account disable/enable is a separate User flag, not a lockout state.
  Unknown usernames are tracked too; successful login keeps the row.
  reset = administrator resets an ordinary member's password.
  limit = current SiteOptions.login_limit.
end note
@enduml
